{
  "id": "grammar.b1.arpadhaz.03.vonatkozoi-nevmas-esetei",
  "title": "Officials and Castles: aki and amely in Descriptions",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "You know *aki* (for people) and *amely* (for things) from A2 Unit 4. Here they describe the county system: the ispán is a person, so he takes *aki*; the castle is a thing, so it takes *amely*. The table gives the phrases you need for the county system."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "The county system",
      "rows": [
        [
          "a vármegye élén az ispán állt",
          "the ispán stood at the head of the county"
        ],
        [
          "a megye székhelye a királyi vár volt",
          "the county seat was the royal castle"
        ],
        [
          "a tatárjárás 1241–1242-ben volt",
          "the Mongol invasion was in 1241–42"
        ],
        [
          "kővárak épültek",
          "stone castles were built"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "title": "Examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "IV. Béla, aki a tatárjárás után újjáépítette az országot, arra ösztönözte a nemeseket, hogy kővárakat építsenek.",
          "english": "Béla IV, who rebuilt the country after the Mongol invasion, urged the nobles to build stone castles."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Az ispán, aki a megye élén állt, a rendért és az adókért felelt.",
          "english": "The ispán, who stood at the head of the county, was responsible for order and taxes."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "A vár, amely a megye székhelye volt, királyi birtok volt.",
          "english": "The castle, which was the county seat, was a royal estate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Ask first whether the word you describe is a person (*aki*, plural *akik*) or a thing (*amely*, plural *amelyek*). The verb in the relative clause agrees with that word."
    }
  ]
}
